#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:10
msgid "Status updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:12
msgid ""
"Status updates ensure that stakeholders remain informed about the "
"playbook run's progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:14
msgid ""
"You can post a status update from the run channel and you can also "
"configure the playbook to send a reminder to post a status update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:18
msgid ""
"To post a status update, access the **Playbooks** tab in Mattermost. "
"Select the run you want to post the update for. In the run details page, "
"select **Post update**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:20
msgid ""
"If this is the first status update and the playbook has a defined "
"template, that template will be pre-populated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:21
msgid ""
"If this is a subsequent status update, the message from the last status "
"update will be pre-populated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:23
msgid "Optionally set a reminder to prompt for the next status update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:25
msgid ""
"If this is the first status update and the playbook has a defined default"
" reminder timer, that timer will be pre-selected here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:26
msgid ""
"If this is a subsequent status update, the last reminder timer will be "
"pre-populated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:28
msgid "Select **Post update** to post your status update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:32
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11.1 and mobile v2.34.0, mobile users can post status "
"updates directly from the Mattermost mobile app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:34
msgid "Open a playbook run from your mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:35
msgid "Select the status update button that appears when viewing the run details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:36
msgid "In the status update modal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:38
msgid ""
"If this is your first status update and the playbook has a status update "
"template, the template content will be pre-populated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:39
msgid ""
"For subsequent updates, your most recent status update content will be "
"pre-populated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:40
msgid ""
"The modal header shows how many people and channels will receive your "
"status update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:42
msgid ""
"Select your reminder timing from the predefined options available in the "
"mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:43
msgid "Select **Post update** to share your status update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:47
msgid ""
"The status update button is only available to participants in the "
"playbook run and is disabled when the run is finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:48
msgid ""
"Mobile time selector options are limited to predefined choices, unlike "
"the web interface which allows custom date entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:50
msgid ""
"When the playbook has a defined broadcast channel, status updates are "
"copied to the broadcast channel as a message from the Playbooks bot. "
"Status updates broadcast to another channel won’t be updated or removed "
"if the original post is edited or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:52
msgid ""
"The most recent status post alsos displays in the right-hand sidebar of "
"the run channel and in the timeline. To correct or remove a status post, "
"edit or delete the post as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:55
msgid "Request an update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:57
msgid ""
"To request a status update, access the **Playbooks** tab in Mattermost. "
"Select the run you want an update for. In the run details page, select "
"the |more-icon-vertical| menu next to **Post update** and select "
"**Request update**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:50
msgid ""
"Use the More icon in the top left corner to access Mattermost desktop "
"apps customization settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:61
msgid ""
"Requesting updates is only available in the web browser and desktop app. "
"This functionality is not available on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:64
msgid "Follow runs and playbooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:66
msgid ""
"Follow specific playbooks to receive updates on important events such as "
"when a run is started and finished, as well as status and retrospective "
"updates every time that playbook is run. This is a good option if you're "
"interested in all instances of a specific workflow, such as an outage "
"resolution playbook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:68
msgid ""
"You can also choose to follow a specific run without actively "
"participating. You’ll receive updates for that run only and can take "
"action if needed. This is useful when you’re only interested in a single "
"instance of a procedure—for example, following onboarding for one "
"specific customer rather than every onboarding run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:72
msgid ""
"Following playbooks and runs is only available in the web browser and "
"desktop app. This functionality is not available on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:75
msgid "Daily digest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:77
msgid ""
"To help you keep track of your runs, tasks, and statuses, a daily digest "
"is sent via direct message in Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:79
msgid ""
"Running playbooks in multiple channels can be overwhelming. The daily "
"digest is sent once a day, in the morning. It lists the actionable items "
"for each run, as well as any outstanding tasks or status updates "
"required. Select the run name to move to that channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:81
msgid ""
"The digest is on by default. To turn it off, use the slash command "
"``/playbook settings digest off``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:84
msgid "Playbook to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/notifications-and-updates.rst:86
msgid ""
"As you complete tasks and finish runs, you can update the details in the "
"digest using the slash command ``/playbook todo``. This slash command can"
" be run in any channel, direct message, or group message. Once run, it "
"delivers an updated digest which includes a list of active runs you "
"belong to."
msgstr ""

